{
  "raw": {
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/949/cw/en/job/589552/night-support-officer-deakin-residential-services": {
      "title": "Night Support Officer, Deakin Residential Services",
      "description": "Night Support Officer, Deakin Residential Services Apply now Job no: 589552 Work type: Part-time Location: Melbourne - Burwood Categories: Customer Service Based at our Melbourne, Burwood Campus Part-time 0.25FTE and continuing HEW 4 $80,046 - $84,849 + 17% Superannuation Why work with us? At Deakin you will have access to benefits such as a variety of leave options including generous parental leave and the ability to purchase additional leave; flexible working arrangements to help manage your work-life balance; ongoing learning and development opportunities to grow your career; an inclusive and supportive culture and environment to work in, both online and on campus. Benefits for working with us! At Deakin, we offer more than just a job - we offer a lifestyle. Across our campuses in Geelong, Melbourne, and regional Victoria, you’ll find everything you need to thrive: on-site childcare, gyms, medical centres, cafes, accessible public transport, and convenient parking. Enjoy flexible working arrangements that support your work-life balance, generous leave entitlements including extended parental leave and the option to purchase additional time off, plus a wide range of staff discounts on travel and more. Our health and wellbeing services, ongoing professional development opportunities, and inclusive, supportive culture make Deakin a place where you can grow - whether you're working remotely or immersed in the vibrant energy of campus life. The role: Deakin Residential Services (DRS) operates as a separate entity that is wholly owned and operated by Deakin University and staffed by University employees. DRS operations are run 24/7, and the team currently manages over 2,900 student beds across multiple campuses – Melbourne Burwood, Geelong Waurn Ponds, Geelong Waterfront and Warrnambool. Based at our Melbourne Burwood campus, the Night Support Officer provides overnight operational, administrative, and customer support to ensure a safe, secure, and well-functioning residential environment. Working independently, the role supports residents, responds to incidents, monitors facilities, and delivers high-quality reception and accommodation services while maintaining accurate records and service continuity. As a Night Support Officer, you will: Assist residents, monitor facilities, respond to incidents, and support reception and short-stay accommodation services, ensuring consistent service delivery during night operations. Respond to enquiries, monitor security and maintenance concerns, and contribute to effective operational outcomes. Apply established processes and exercise judgement to deliver consistent outcomes Analyse information from available sources to support task completion and provide input to decision-making Contribute to team effectiveness through communication and collaboration To be successful, you’ll have: Diploma qualification with relevant experience; or certificate level qualification with post certificate work experience, or Post-Trades Certificate or Advanced Certificate or an equivalent combination of experience and/or education/training Experience in administrative or operational roles as well as working with systems and processes Ability to apply judgement to prioritise work and manage competing priorities Strong communication and interpersonal skills Here's how to apply: Please submit your updated resume and a short cover letter outlining your skills and experience. For a confidential discussion regarding this role, please contact Krystle Pricop (Senior Coordinator, Residential Experience) on k.pricop@deakin.edu.au. For a copy of the position description, please see below: PD - Night Support Officer 589552.pdf Applications for this position close on Monday 26th October at 11:55pm. Are You Ready? Deakin is a Victorian university with a global impact. We are an agile, dynamic, and innovative university committed to making a positive impact through our excellence in education, research and innovation and the contributions we make to the wider community. We understand that our reputation has been built on the dedication and expertise of our staff and we offer a dynamic and diverse working environment with opportunities to grow and develop careers. We believe that a progressive, thriving culture will ensure that people choose to come, and stay at Deakin and contribute to our ongoing success. We value diversity and aim to build an inclusive environment that champions, embraces and respects differences. We support and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, and people of all abilities, cultures, sexual orientation, and genders. Pre-employment safety and suitability checks: In accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence, appointment to this role is subject to successful completion of relevant pre-employment checks, including Working With Children Checks and candidate gender-based violence declarations. Candidates may be asked to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender‑based Violence, or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender‑based Violence during the course of their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process. A declaration is not required from individuals who have experienced gender‑based violence. A ‘Yes’ response does not automatically exclude a candidate from employment, and any information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for relevance to the role and the University’s safety obligations. Advertised: 12 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 26 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/949/cw/en/job/589844/senior-consultant-business-development": {
      "title": "Senior Consultant, Business Development",
      "description": "Senior Consultant, Business Development Apply now Job no: 589844 Work type: Full-time Location: Flexible Categories: Management Flexible location + hybrid work arrangements Full-time and continuing $143,627 - $152,229 (HEW 9) + 17% superannuation Make an Impact Build relationships with industry and government partners, connecting their priorities and challenges with Deakin's research expertise. Work alongside researchers to identify and pursue opportunities for externally funded research and commercialisation. Help turn promising research ideas into successful partnerships, drawing on expertise from across the University. What You Will Deliver Develop and manage a portfolio of business development opportunities, building a strong pipeline of prospective partnerships and research funding. Provide clear, practical advice to researchers and senior leaders, helping them assess opportunities and make informed decisions. Coordinate complex proposals and partnership activity, bringing teams together and ensuring University requirements are met. About the Team You’ll join Deakin’s Business Development and Commercialisation function, a collaborative team connecting researchers with industry, government and other partners to create new research opportunities and bring innovative ideas into practice. The broader function brings together expertise across business development, intellectual property, commercialisation and entrepreneurship, including Deakin’s Recycling and Clean Energy Commercialisation Hub (REACH). You may be a great fit for this role if you: Bring extensive relevant experience and postgraduate qualifications, or an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Have led functions, programs or significant bodies of work, managing resources and delivering results in complex environments. Build strong relationships with industry, government and research stakeholders, with the confidence to influence decisions and develop opportunities for collaboration. Bring strong analytical and problem-solving skills, turning complex information into clear, practical advice. Understand governance and policy requirements, and bring a proactive, collaborative approach to improving how work gets done. Apply today : Please submit your current resume and a short covering letter outlining your skills and experience. Want to Know More? For a confidential discussion, or for further questions regarding this role, please contact Emma Prime (Associate Director, Business Development, REACH) via emma.prime@deakin.edu.au For a copy of the position description, please see below: Senior Consultant, Business Development.pdf Applications for this position close at 11:55 pm on Friday 23 October 2026 Deakin at a Glance Deakin is a globally recognised university committed to making a positive impact through education, research and innovation. Our success is driven by our people, and we're dedicated to creating a workplace where individuals feel supported, valued and empowered to do their best work. We offer a collaborative and inclusive culture, opportunities for professional growth, and the flexibility to balance work and life. We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds and are committed to building a diverse workforce that reflects the communities we serve. What We Offer At Deakin , you'll be supported to thrive both professionally and personally. We offer flexible working arrangements, competitive salary and superannuation benefits, wellbeing initiatives, generous leave provisions, and professional development opportunities to help you achieve your career goals. Join a collaborative and inclusive community that values innovation, flexibility, diversity, and making a positive impact through education, research, and engagement. To find out why our staff love working with Deakin, read more here ! Pre-employment safety and suitability checks: As part of Deakin's commitment to providing a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, successful candidates will be required to complete relevant pre-employment checks, which include a Working with Children Check and declarations relating to gender-based violence in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. Any information provided will be treated confidentially and assessed only where relevant to the requirements of the role and Deakin's duty of care obligations. A declaration does not automatically preclude a candidate from employment. Advertised: 12 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 23 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/949/cw/en/job/589622/reception-officer": {
      "title": "Reception Officer",
      "description": "Reception Officer Apply now Job no: 589622 Work type: Part-time Location: Warrnambool Categories: Customer Service Based at our Warrnambool Campus Part-time 0.6 FTE and continuing (flexible ordinary hour span) $80,046 - $84,849 (HEW 4) + 17% Superannuation (pro rata part time) Why this role matters This is an opportunity to be the friendly first point of contact for Deakin Residential Services and help create a welcoming, supportive residential community in Warrnambool. As Reception Officer, you will provide exceptional customer service and administrative support to current and prospective residents, families, university staff and contractors, while assisting with programs, events and day-to-day residential operations. Reporting to the Senior Coordinator, Deakin Residential Services Operations, you will play an important role in ensuring residents receive timely information, support and referrals, contributing to a positive student experience and vibrant residential community. This position is rostered for 7:00am to 3:00pm on Wednesdays and Thursdays, and 9:00am to 5:00pm on Sundays. As a Reception Officer you will: Be the first point of contact that matters - deliver welcoming, reliable reception and administrative support to residents, families, staff and contractors. Create outstanding customer experiences by responding quickly to enquiries, resolving issues and connecting people with the right services. Bring ideas to the table - embrace continuous improvement, adapt to change and help refine processes that make services more accessible and efficient. Thrive in a collaborative, inclusive team – communicate clearly, build strong relationships and support colleagues to deliver shared outcomes. Stay organised and proactive - manage daily tasks, track progress and balance priorities to keep operations running smoothly in a busy residential environment. To be successful, you’ll have: Completion of an Associate Diploma level qualifications with relevant work experience or a certificate level qualification with post-certificate relevant work experience; or Completion of a post-Trades Certificate or Advanced Certificate and extensive relevant and on the job training; or An equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education/training This position is designated a flexible ordinary hours span position due to operational needs. A 20% flexible loading applies to every hour worked outside the University Ordinary Hours of Work. Information about Flexible Ordinary Hours Span can be found in the Deakin Enterprise Agreement under Clause 43. Here's how to apply: Please submit your updated resume and a short cover letter outlining your skills and experience. For a confidential discussion regarding this role, please contact Ryan Manson (Senior Coordinator, Deakin Residential Service Operations) on r.manson@deakin.edu.au For a copy of the position description, please see below: PD - Reception Officer, 589622.pdf Applications for this position close on Friday 23rd October at 11:55pm. Benefits for working with us! At Deakin, we offer more than just a job. We offer a rewarding career in a flexible, inclusive and forward-thinking environment. Across our campuses in Geelong, Melbourne and regional Victoria, you'll enjoy flexible working arrangements that support work-life balance, generous leave provisions including extended parental leave and the option to purchase additional leave, and access to a range of professional development opportunities to help you grow your career. Are You Ready? Deakin is a Victorian university with a global impact. We are an agile, dynamic, and innovative university committed to making a positive impact through our excellence in education, research and innovation and the contributions we make to the wider community. We understand that our reputation has been built on the dedication and expertise of our staff and we offer a dynamic and diverse working environment with opportunities to grow and develop careers. We believe that a progressive, thriving culture will ensure that people choose to come, and stay at Deakin and contribute to our ongoing success. We value diversity and aim to build an inclusive environment that champions, embraces and respects differences. We support and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, and people of all abilities, cultures, sexual orientation, and genders. Pre-employment safety and suitability checks: In accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence, appointment to this role is subject to successful completion of relevant pre-employment checks, including Working With Children Checks and candidate gender-based violence declarations. Candidates may be asked to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender‑based Violence, or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender‑based Violence during the course of their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process. A declaration is not required from individuals who have experienced gender‑based violence. A ‘Yes’ response does not automatically exclude a candidate from employment, and any information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for relevance to the role and the University’s safety obligations. Advertised: 09 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/949/cw/en/job/589736/senior-coordinator-campaigns": {
      "title": "Senior Coordinator, Campaigns",
      "description": "Senior Coordinator, Campaigns Apply now Job no: 589736 Work type: Full-time Location: Flexible, Geelong - City, Melbourne - Burwood Categories: Marketing and Communications Based at either Melbourne Burwood or Geelong Waterfront Campus + hybrid work arrangements 16-month fixed-term opportunity until 31 January 2028 $123,554- $141,459 (HEW8) + 17% Superannuation Why this role matters Join Deakin and help bring groundbreaking research to life through bold campaigns, compelling storytelling and impactful digital experiences that showcase the University's research excellence. As Senior Coordinator, Campaigns, you will lead the delivery of integrated marketing campaigns that elevate the profile and impact of Deakin's research. Working across strategy, content and digital marketing, you will translate ideas into engaging campaigns that connect with diverse audiences and strengthen Deakin's reputation as a leading research institution. Leading a talented team of marketing professionals, you will set priorities, guide delivery and foster a collaborative, high-performing culture. You'll work closely with researchers, senior leaders and stakeholders across the University to deliver innovative marketing initiatives and measurable outcomes. This is an exciting opportunity for a strategic and hands-on marketing leader who thrives in a fast-paced environment and enjoys turning ambitious ideas into high-impact campaigns. Through this 16-month fixed-term opportunity, you'll help shape how Deakin's research is shared, celebrated and amplified to audiences locally and globally. As a Senior Coordinator, Campaigns you will: Lead the planning and delivery of integrated marketing campaigns that elevate the profile and impact of Deakin's research. Manage and develop a multidisciplinary team delivering content, storytelling, digital, social media and campaign activity. Drive audience-focused marketing initiatives informed by data, insights and performance outcomes. Build strong relationships with stakeholders across the University and external partners to deliver strategic objectives. Identify opportunities to improve team effectiveness, optimising processes, prioritisation, reporting and campaign delivery. To be successful, you’ll have: Demonstrated experience leading integrated marketing campaigns and content initiatives from strategy through to delivery. Proven ability to lead, motivate and develop high-performing teams in a fast-paced and collaborative environment. Strong stakeholder management skills, with the ability to influence, build partnerships and navigate competing priorities. Experience using audience insights, digital analytics and performance data to inform decisions and optimise outcomes. Exceptional communication, project management and organisational skills, with a track record of delivering high-quality results. Here's how to apply: Please submit your updated resume and a short cover letter outlining your skills and experience. For a confidential discussion regarding this role, please contact Erin Thornback (Research Marketing Manager) on e.thornback@deakin.edu.au For a copy of the position description, please see below: PD - Senior Coordinator Campaigns_589736.pdf Applications for this position close on Thursday 22nd October at 11:55pm. Benefits for working with us! At Deakin, we offer more than just a job. We offer a rewarding career in a flexible, inclusive and forward-thinking environment. Across our campuses in Geelong, Melbourne and regional Victoria, you'll enjoy flexible working arrangements that support work-life balance, generous leave provisions including extended parental leave and the option to purchase additional leave, and access to a range of professional development opportunities to help you grow your career. Are You Ready? Deakin is a Victorian university with a global impact. We are an agile, dynamic, and innovative university committed to making a positive impact through our excellence in education, research and innovation and the contributions we make to the wider community. We understand that our reputation has been built on the dedication and expertise of our staff and we offer a dynamic and diverse working environment with opportunities to grow and develop careers. We believe that a progressive, thriving culture will ensure that people choose to come, and stay at Deakin and contribute to our ongoing success. We value diversity and aim to build an inclusive environment that champions, embraces and respects differences. We support and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, and people of all abilities, cultures, sexual orientation, and genders. Pre-employment safety and suitability checks: In accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence, appointment to this role is subject to successful completion of relevant pre-employment checks, including Working With Children Checks and candidate gender-based violence declarations. Candidates may be asked to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender‑based Violence, or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender‑based Violence during the course of their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process. A declaration is not required from individuals who have experienced gender‑based violence. A ‘Yes’ response does not automatically exclude a candidate from employment, and any information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for relevance to the role and the University’s safety obligations. Advertised: 09 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
