    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/949/cw/en/job/589840/expression-of-interest-graduate-researcher-teaching-fellow-humanities-and-social-sciences": {
      "title": "Expression of Interest, Graduate Researcher Teaching Fellow, Humanities and Social Sciences.",
      "description": "Expression of Interest, Graduate Researcher Teaching Fellow, Humanities and Social Sciences. Apply now Job no: 589840 Work type: Part-time Location: Flexible, Geelong - City, Geelong - Waurn Ponds, Melbourne - Burwood Categories: Arts, Education, Teaching Innovation Support, Educational Design, Course Enhancement Are you a graduate researcher ready to gain teaching experience alongside your research as you build your academic career? The School of Humanities and Social Sciences is inviting expressions of interest in Graduate Researcher Teaching Fellow positions across a range of disciplines. You can nominate one or more areas that align with your research and academic interests. If successful, you will be aligned with one of our disciplines. These fixed-term positions provide an opportunity to gain practical teaching experience, become part of the academic life of the School, and develop skills that will support your future academic career. Graduate Researcher Teaching Fellows are typically involved in teaching seminars and marking of undergraduate units. Flexible location Fixed Term, 0.10 FTE – 0.5FTE (7.35 – 18.37 hours per week. Full-time candidates require Faculty GR Director approval to exceed a fixed-term teaching fraction of 0.2 FTE. Total hours per contract may be worked as needed to accommodate workload peaks & troughs, provided total hours worked align with the employment contract amount.) Level A $86,599 - $116,417 + 17% Superannuation (pro rata, part time) Why work with us? At Deakin you will have access to a range of benefits including paid wellbeing leave, personal leave and recreation leave; flexible working arrangements to help manage your work-life balance; access to learning and development opportunities to support your career growth; an inclusive and supportive culture and environment to work in, both online and on campus. Available disciplines: Anthropology Criminology History International Relations Middle East Studies Humanitarian Development and International Studies Philosophy Politics Sociology As a Graduate Researcher Teaching Fellow, you will: Deliver and provide innovative and effective teaching practices to enhance student success and engagement, while maintaining a focus on continuous improvement. Contribute to the development of high-quality learning materials, activities, and assessments, working collaboratively with the Unit Chair and teaching team to support curriculum innovation. Integrate industry (if relevant) and research practices into student learning experiences, ensuring relevance and practical application of knowledge. Provide constructive feedback on student performance using clear assessment criteria and actively contribute to moderation processes to ensure consistency and quality of assessment and feedback. Engage in professional development opportunities and maintain a commitment to educational excellence. To be successful, you’ll have: Currently enrolled in a graduate research degree, MRes or PhD, at Deakin University in a relevant and related discipline. Demonstrated satisfactory progress towards timely completion and have approval from supervisor to apply for the position. Demonstrated passion for teaching and learning. Excellent organisational skills, effective time management skills, and the ability to manage multiple tasks simultaneously and meet deadlines successfully. Demonstrated experience in or demonstrable ability to deliver effective teaching that improves student success and engagement across a range of modes of delivery. Capacity to contribute to teaching-related administration including the ability to interpret and understand policies and procedures relevant to teaching and student support and welfare. Excellent interpersonal skills and a proven ability to establish good working relationships with colleagues and students. Emerging record of scholarly learning and teaching in undergraduate programs. Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal, for use with staff and students. Here's how to apply: Please complete the application form and submit your current resume. This will be considered as an expression of interest in these roles in principle. If successful, we will discuss with you an appropriate fraction (ranging from 0.1 FTE to 0.5 FTE) based on the work available, your study load, and the constraints of your candidature. For a confidential discussion about this role, please contact AHoS Operations, Associate Professor Chris Mayes - christopher.mayes@deakin.edu.au For a copy of the position description, please see below: PD - Graduate Researcher Teaching Fellow.pdf Applications for this position close on Friday the 30th of October. Are You Ready? Deakin is a Victorian university with a global impact. We are an agile, dynamic, and innovative university committed to making a positive impact through our excellence in education, research and innovation and the contributions we make to the wider community. We understand that our reputation has been built on the dedication and expertise of our staff and we offer a dynamic and diverse working environment with opportunities to grow and develop careers. We believe that a progressive, thriving culture will ensure that people choose to come, and stay at Deakin and contribute to our ongoing success. We value diversity and aim to build an inclusive environment that champions, embraces and respects differences. We support and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, and people of all abilities, cultures, sexual orientation, and genders. Pre-employment safety and suitability checks: In accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence, appointment to this role is subject to successful completion of relevant pre-employment checks, including Working With Children Checks and candidate gender-based violence declarations . Candidates may be asked to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender ‑ based Violence, or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender‑ based Violence during the course of their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process . A declaration is not required from individuals who have experienced gender‑ based violence . A ‘Yes’ response does not automatically exclude a candidate from employment, and any information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for relevance to the role and the University’s safety obligations. Advertised: 09 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 30 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/949/cw/en/job/589848/school-administration-officer": {
      "title": "School Administration Officer",
      "description": "School Administration Officer Apply now Job no: 589848 Work type: Full-time Location: Melbourne - Burwood Categories: Administration Based at our Melbourne, Burwood Campus + hybrid work arrangements Full-time and continuing HEW 5 $86,744 - $97,290 + 17% Superannuation Why work with us? At Deakin you will have access to benefits such as a variety of leave options including generous parental leave and the ability to purchase additional leave; flexible working arrangements to help manage your work-life balance; ongoing learning and development opportunities to grow your career; an inclusive and supportive culture and environment to work in, both online and on campus. Who are we? Deakin is a cutting-edge public university headquartered in Victoria, revolutionising education with 61,000 students across our campuses: Melbourne Burwood, Geelong Waurn Ponds, Geelong Waterfront, Warrnambool, Deakin University Lancaster University Indonesia (DLI), GIFT City, India, and our vibrant online environment. We're proud to be a progressive and open-minded university, delivering the highest student satisfaction in Victoria and consistently ranked in the top 1% of the world's universities. As a School Administrative Officer in the Deakin Law School you will: Provide responsive administrative support across Deakin Law School, assisting academic staff and stakeholders with day-to-day enquiries and activities Serve as the virtual reception for the Deakin Law Clinics, responding professionally to enquiries from prospective clients and coordinating appointments Support the operational planning and preparation of the School and the Law Clinics for each trimester Coordinate administrative processes supporting the School’s teaching and research program To be successful, you’ll have: Degree without subsequent experience; or Diploma with experience; or Post Trades Certificate/Advanced Certificate with relevant experience; or equivalent combination of experience and/or education/training Experience providing advice or support services Strong communication and stakeholder engagement skills Ability to interpret and apply procedures Experience coordinating work and managing priorities Here's how to apply: Please submit your updated resume and a short cover letter outlining your skills and experience. For a confidential discussion regarding this role, please contact John Janetzki (School Manager) on dls-sm@deakin.edu.au For a copy of the position description, please see below: PD - School Administration Officer 589848.pdf Applications for this position close on 25 October 2026. Are You Ready? Deakin is a Victorian university with a global impact. We are an agile, dynamic, and innovative university committed to making a positive impact through our excellence in education, research and innovation and the contributions we make to the wider community. We understand that our reputation has been built on the dedication and expertise of our staff and we offer a dynamic and diverse working environment with opportunities to grow and develop careers. We believe that a progressive, thriving culture will ensure that people choose to come, and stay at Deakin and contribute to our ongoing success. We value diversity and aim to build an inclusive environment that champions, embraces and respects differences. We support and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, and people of all abilities, cultures, sexual orientation, and genders. Pre-employment safety and suitability checks: In accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence, appointment to this role is subject to successful completion of relevant pre-employment checks, including Working With Children Checks and candidate gender-based violence declarations. Candidates may be asked to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender‑based Violence, or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender‑based Violence during the course of their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process. A declaration is not required from individuals who have experienced gender‑based violence. A ‘Yes’ response does not automatically exclude a candidate from employment, and any information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for relevance to the role and the University’s safety obligations. Advertised: 09 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 25 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
